NAME
    gcloud alpha apihub discovered-api-observations - manage Discovered Api
        Observation resources

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha apihub discovered-api-observations GROUP | COMMAND
        [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Manage Discovered Api Observation resources.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --help.

    Run $ gcloud help for details.

GROUPS
    GROUP is one of the following:

     discovered-api-operations
        (ALPHA) Manage Discovered Api Operation resources.

COMMANDS
    COMMAND is one of the following:

     describe
        (ALPHA) Describe a Discovered Api Observation.

     list
        (ALPHA) List Discovered Api Observations.

NOTES
    This command is currently in alpha and might change without notice. If this
    command fails with API permission errors despite specifying the correct
    project, you might be trying to access an API with an invitation-only early
    access allowlist. This variant is also available:

        $ gcloud apihub discovered-api-observations

